environments/prod/automation.ork.yaml  namespace payments
~ namespace  payments
      description: "" → "card rails"
      allowed_pools: [] → ["main"]
+ trigger    github-deploy      deploy@current
      orkflow: "deploy"
      description: "GitHub Actions deploy hook"
~ schedule   nightly-reconcile  reconcile@current  0 2 * * * (Europe/Lisbon)  sch-<id>
      cron: ["0 3 * * *"] → ["0 2 * * *"]
~ webhook    etl-loader         https://hooks.acme.dev/etl  payments/nightly-etl/*  wh-<id>
      orkflow: "" → "nightly-etl"
? trigger    manual-hook        deploy@current  trg-<id>  not in this document; kept (--prune deletes it)
! trigger    -                  deploy@current  trg-<id>  has no name; name it with `orkctl trigger update trg-<id> -n payments --name NAME` to manage it here

Plan: 1 to create, 3 to update, 0 to delete.
Plan digest: sha256:<digest>

Applied 4 of 4 steps in namespace payments.
  applied   ~ namespace  payments
  applied   + trigger    github-deploy      trg-<id>
  applied   ~ schedule   nightly-reconcile
  applied   ~ webhook    etl-loader

Trigger github-deploy (trg-<id>) was created. Its token is shown once:
  <secret>
Invoke it with:
  curl -X POST 'http://localhost:8080/v1/triggers/trg-<id>' \
    -H 'Authorization: Bearer <secret>' \
    -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
    -d '{}'
  # optional: -H 'Ork-Origin-Reference: <your CI job URL>' records a correlation reference on the run
